    "field": "Cloud-radiation-dynamics interactions",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the significant uncertainty in climate projections stemming from a poor understanding of how midlatitude atmospheric dynamics, clouds, and radiation interact, challenging the assumption that circulation changes like jet shifts are the primary drivers of extratropical cloud feedbacks under global warming.",
    "method": "This review paper uses regression analysis to isolate the component of the cloud-radiative response related to jet stream shifts, separating the dynamical contribution from the total cloud feedback under global warming to determine the dominant processes.",
    "task": "This paper reviews the scientific understanding of how midlatitude atmospheric dynamics interact with clouds and radiation, and discusses the implications of these connections for cloud feedbacks in a warming climate.",
